  sit_title: "What happened on 4 October 2026",
  sit_intro: "Brazil held the first round of its presidential election. Voting is compulsory and ballots are cast on electronic machines (urnas eletrônicas); the electoral authority TSE publishes final results per section — 499,248 of them, each covering a few hundred voters. Nobody crossed 50%, so the two leaders meet again in a runoff.",
