  fig1_cap: "I set the high-turnout cutoff at 91.6%: the 99.5th percentile, meaning only about 0.5% of sections have higher turnout. Those sections hold 0.62% of all ballots, 0.49% of Flávio Bolsonaro’s votes and 0.80% of Lula’s. This counts votes above a chosen line; it cannot identify fake votes or set a limit on their number. Choosing a percentile ensures that only a small share of sections lies above it.",
  fig1_alt: "Turnout histogram: one smooth bell near 80%, boundary at 91.6%",
  fig2_cap: "Across Brazil, higher turnout has little link with either candidate’s vote share: the weighted correlation is −0.03 for Flávio Bolsonaro and +0.05 for Lula. Adding fake votes can sometimes create a rising tail on this chart. A link would not prove fraud, and a value near zero does not rule it out. Geography and the way areas are combined can also change the pattern.",
